<title>TURKEY: Turk Cukurova Elektrik Q1 net up 83 pct.</title>
<headline>Turk Cukurova Elektrik Q1 net up 83 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan-March 1997 provisional</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira) 3,698.21 vs   2,022.72</p>
<p>    Net profit		  1,849.11 vs   1,011.36</p>
<p>    Net sales		  10,601.86 vs   5,384.15</p>
<p>    Operating profit	  3,219.65 vs   2,502.80</p>
<p>    Exceptional income	  361.72 vs     505.28</p>
<p>    Exceptional expense	 203.55 vs     427.18</p>
<p>    Interest paid	     1,252.90 vs   1,016.30</p>
<p>    Total debts		28,407.38 vs  18,126.79</p>
<p>    Equity			6,754.01 vs   3,691.28</p>
<p>    Capital			 500.00 vs     500.00</p>
<p>NOTE - Cukurova Elektrik A.S. is Turkey's biggest private sector utility controlled by the Rumeli group. It produces and distributes electricity in the southern Cukurova region.</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 77 percent annual wholesale inflation in March.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-2750875.</p>
</text>
